+---
+title: "best-open-source-ai-agents-2026"
+description: "Discover the best open source AI agents for 2026: verified GitHub repos for coding, browser automation, self-hosting, RAG, and workflow stacks."
+icon: 📋
+category: artificial-intelligence
+---
+
+# Best Open Source AI Agents 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-open-source-ai-agents-2026?style=social)
+
+> Best open source AI agents 2026 is a curated list of verified GitHub repositories for coding agents, browser agents, self-hosted assistants, agent frameworks, and workflow automation stacks. Every tool below has a public `github.com` repository, avoids SaaS-only lock-in, and includes a research snapshot for stars, language, license, and recent commit activity.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
+- [License](#license)
+
+## TL;DR
+- `google-gemini/gemini-cli`, `block/goose`, and `langchain-ai/open-swe` are the strongest picks for developer-focused AI agents.
+- `bytedance/UI-TARS-desktop`, `nanobrowser/nanobrowser`, and `magnitudedev/browser-agent` stand out for browser and computer-use automation.
+- `mudler/LocalAI`, `danny-avila/LibreChat`, and `eosphoros-ai/DB-GPT` are solid self-hosted options when privacy and infrastructure control matter.
+- `google/adk-python`, `VoltAgent/voltagent`, and `TEN-framework/ten-framework` are useful foundations if you want to build your own multi-agent products.
+- Gap note: narrow query slices such as `free ai agents github` and `ai agents MIT license` returned fewer than five repos in the supplied research, so this list groups tools by practical use case instead.
+
+## Why This List
+The best open source AI agents are increasingly useful because teams want agent workflows they can inspect, self-host, modify, and integrate into their own infrastructure. A GitHub-first awesome list is the cleanest way to separate real open source projects from marketing-heavy SaaS wrappers, closed demos, and cloud-only products that do not give builders meaningful control.
+
+## Open Source Tools
+
+### Agent Frameworks And SDKs
+
+#### [Google Agent Development Kit for Python](https://github.com/google/adk-python)
+> **Description:** `adk-python` is Google’s Python toolkit for building multi-agent systems with structured tools, sessions, memory, and deployment primitives. The project is useful when you want a framework-level foundation rather than a finished assistant, and its repository activity shows steady maintenance around runtime behavior, tool execution, and release management. It is Apache-2.0 licensed and aimed at developers who want to compose agent behaviors in Python applications. In this research snapshot it had 18,659 stars, Python as the primary language, Apache License 2.0, and the latest visible commit on Mar 18, 2026.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/google/adk-python](https://github.com/google/adk-python)
+- **Stars:** 18659 ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** Mar 18, 2026
+- **Category:** framework, multi-agent, sdk
+- **Best for:** Building Python-native agent systems with sessions and tools
+
+---
+
+#### [Google Agent Development Kit for Go](https://github.com/google/adk-go)
+> **Description:** `adk-go` brings the same agent-building model into the Go ecosystem for teams that want stronger concurrency control, static typing, and backend-oriented deployments. The repo emphasizes agent orchestration, tool confirmation, remote agent patterns, and production-friendly code organization. It is a good fit for Go shops that want to add agent capabilities without adopting a Python-first stack. In this research snapshot it had 7,290 stars, Go as the primary language, Apache License 2.0, and the latest visible commit on Mar 3, 2026.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/google/adk-go](https://github.com/google/adk-go)
+- **Stars:** 7290 ⭐
+- **Language:** Go
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** Mar 3, 2026
+- **Category:** framework, go, sdk
+- **Best for:** Backend teams building typed agent services in Go
+
+---
+
+#### [VoltAgent](https://github.com/VoltAgent/voltagent)
+> **Description:** `voltagent` is a TypeScript agent framework for building application-grade AI agents with a modern Node.js developer experience. Its README and commit history position it as a practical foundation for prompt management, telemetry, context handling, and extensible agent execution rather than a toy chat wrapper. Teams that already ship JavaScript or TypeScript services can use it to build custom agents with lower friction. In this research snapshot it had 7,108 stars, TypeScript as the primary language, MIT License, and the latest visible commit on Mar 21, 2026.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/VoltAgent/voltagent](https://github.com/VoltAgent/voltagent)
+- **Stars:** 7108 ⭐
+- **Language:** TypeScript
+- **License:** MIT
+- **Last Commit:** Mar 21, 2026
+- **Category:** framework, typescript, developer-tools
+- **Best for:** Shipping custom TypeScript agents inside existing products
+
+---
+
+#### [TEN Framework](https://github.com/TEN-framework/ten-framework)
+> **Description:** `ten-framework` is an open framework for real-time multimodal agents and agentic applications. The repository is especially interesting for teams working on voice, streaming interaction, or graph-based orchestration because it goes beyond plain text workflows and focuses on production-oriented runtime pieces. Its Python-centered implementation and Apache licensing make it accessible for experimentation and enterprise evaluation alike. In this research snapshot it had 10,377 stars, Python as the primary language, Apache License 2.0, and the latest visible commit on Mar 10, 2026.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/TEN-framework/ten-framework](https://github.com/TEN-framework/ten-framework)
+- **Stars:** 10377 ⭐
+- **Language:** Python
+- **License:** Other
+- **Last Commit:** Mar 10, 2026
+- **Category:** framework, realtime, multimodal
+- **Best for:** Real-time and multimodal agent infrastructure
+
+---
+
+#### [AgentSet](https://github.com/agentset-ai/agentset)
+> **Description:** `agentset` is a lighter-weight TypeScript-first framework for composing and deploying agents without forcing a heavy platform abstraction. The repository leans toward developer ergonomics, examples, and reusable building blocks, which makes it appealing for startups and smaller teams that want control without a large framework surface area. It is MIT licensed and well suited to custom agent products where fast iteration matters more than a giant ecosystem. In this research snapshot it had 1,932 stars, TypeScript as the primary language, MIT License, and the latest visible commit on Feb 15, 2026.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/agentset-ai/agentset](https://github.com/agentset-ai/agentset)
+- **Stars:** 1932 ⭐
+- **Language:** TypeScript
+- **License:** MIT
+- **Last Commit:** Feb 15, 2026
+- **Category:** framework, typescript, starter-kit
+- **Best for:** Small teams building custom app-specific agents
+
+---
+
+### Coding And Developer Agents
+
+#### [Gemini CLI](https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli)
+> **Description:** `gemini-cli` is a high-traction open source coding agent that turns the terminal into an agent workspace with planning, tool use, file operations, and browser-oriented capabilities. The repository is notably active, with frequent changes across core agent behavior, MCP discovery, browser settings, and sandbox management. It is one of the clearest examples of a developer-facing open source AI agent in 2026. In this research snapshot it had 99,498 stars, TypeScript as the primary language, Apache License 2.0, and the latest visible commit on Mar 25, 2026.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli](https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli)
+- **Stars:** 99498 ⭐
+- **Language:** TypeScript
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** Mar 25, 2026
+- **Category:** coding-agent, cli, developer-tools
+- **Best for:** Terminal-first code generation and repo automation
+
+---
+
+#### [Qwen Code](https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code)
+> **Description:** `qwen-code` is an open source coding agent and CLI around Qwen’s code-focused models, aimed at code editing, project navigation, and developer workflows. It is a useful option if you want a public GitHub repository with strong model alignment toward software tasks and an Apache-style licensing posture. The project is especially attractive to teams already experimenting with open model stacks and code assistants. In this research snapshot it had 21,309 stars, TypeScript as the primary language, Apache License 2.0, and recent activity reflected the Mar 2026 research window.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code](https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code)
+- **Stars:** 21309 ⭐
+- **Language:** TypeScript
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** Mar 2026 snapshot
+- **Category:** coding-agent, cli, open-models
+- **Best for:** Developers who want an open coding agent around Qwen models
+
+---
+
+#### [Goose](https://github.com/block/goose)
+> **Description:** `goose` is Block’s open source AI agent for engineering workflows, combining a desktop- and terminal-friendly experience with support for tools, project context, and iterative problem solving. The repo is substantial and clearly maintained, with active work spanning docs, dependency management, and product polish. For developers who want a polished open source alternative to closed coding agents, Goose is one of the strongest repos to watch. In this research snapshot it had 33,743 stars, Rust as the primary language, Apache License 2.0, and the latest visible commit on Mar 29, 2026.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/block/goose](https://github.com/block/goose)
+- **Stars:** 33743 ⭐
+- **Language:** Rust
+- **License:** Apache-2.0
+- **Last Commit:** Mar 29, 2026
+- **Category:** coding-agent, rust, desktop
+- **Best for:** Engineers wanting a polished open source coding assistant
+
