+## TL;DR
+- `google-gemini/gemini-cli`, `block/goose`, and `langchain-ai/open-swe` are the strongest picks for developer-focused AI agents.
+- `bytedance/UI-TARS-desktop`, `nanobrowser/nanobrowser`, and `magnitudedev/browser-agent` stand out for browser and computer-use automation.
+- `mudler/LocalAI`, `danny-avila/LibreChat`, and `eosphoros-ai/DB-GPT` are solid self-hosted options when privacy and infrastructure control matter.
+- `google/adk-python`, `VoltAgent/voltagent`, and `TEN-framework/ten-framework` are useful foundations if you want to build your own multi-agent products.
+- Gap note: narrow query slices such as `free ai agents github` and `ai agents MIT license` returned fewer than five repos in the supplied research, so this list groups tools by practical use case instead.
+
+## Why This List
+The best open source AI agents are increasingly useful because teams want agent workflows they can inspect, self-host, modify, and integrate into their own infrastructure. A GitHub-first awesome list is the cleanest way to separate real open source projects from marketing-heavy SaaS wrappers, closed demos, and cloud-only products that do not give builders meaningful control.
